{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1717","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Madoka and Strange Thoughts"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Madoka is a very strange girl, and therefore she suddenly wondered how many pairs of integers $$$(a, b)$$$ exist, where $$$1 \\leq a, b \\leq n$$$, for which $$$\\frac{\\operatorname{lcm}(a, b)}{\\operatorname{gcd}(a, b)} \\leq 3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this problem, $$$\\operatorname{gcd}(a, b)$$$ denotes "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greatest_common_divisor "},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"the greatest common divisor"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the numbers $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$, and $$$\\operatorname{lcm}(a, b)$$$ denotes "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Least_common_multiple "},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"the smallest common multiple"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the numbers $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The input consists of multiple test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases. Description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and the only line of each test case contains the integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^8$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case output a single integer — the number of pairs of integers satisfying the condition."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n1\n2\n3\n4\n5\n100000000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n4\n7\n10\n11\n266666666\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For $$$n = 1$$$ there is exactly one pair of numbers — $$$(1, 1)$$$ and it fits."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For $$$n = 2$$$, there are only $$$4$$$ pairs — $$$(1, 1)$$$, $$$(1, 2)$$$, $$$(2, 1)$$$, $$$(2, 2)$$$ and they all fit."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For $$$n = 3$$$, all $$$9$$$ pair are suitable, except $$$(2, 3)$$$ and $$$(3, 2)$$$, since their $$$\\operatorname{lcm}$$$ is $$$6$$$, and $$$\\operatorname{gcd}$$$ is $$$1$$$, which doesn't fit the condition."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1717A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1717/problem/A"}